# Optional. Copy to `.env` only if this engagement needs one.
#
# ⚠️ Most builds do NOT need this file at all. The default is a local model
# through Ollama, which has no key and no account — that is the entire pitch.
# `docker-compose.yml` marks it `required: false` for exactly that reason.
#
# `.env` is read from the HOST at run time and is never baked into the image.
# Never commit a filled-in copy.

# Names the image and the container, so two engagements on one machine do not
# collide. Lower-case, no spaces.
#CLIENT_SLUG=acme

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BRING-YOUR-OWN-KEY BUILDS ONLY.
#
# Set this ONLY when `client.toml` has `[model] kind = "byok"` — that is, when
# the client's hardware could not run a useful model and they chose, in writing,
# to send their documents to a provider they pay directly.
#
# The variable NAME must match `api_key_env` in their `client.toml`. The key
# itself lives here and only here, never in the config file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#OPENAI_API_KEY=
#GOOGLE_API_KEY=
